almost three and a half decades have  passed since the murder of daniel morgan  outside an ordinary pub in southeast  london  but this is a far from ordinary case at  his heart allegations of police  corruption  of criminal networks collusion with  tabloid journalists  and a family whose fight for answers has  been frustrated  at every turn i've had enough of them  i've had enough in british policing to  be quite honest you know after  after 34 years of it aleister morgan  knows it's now highly unlikely anyone  will ever be brought to justice for his  brother's murder  but an independent report he hopes may  finally shed some light on a case  that continues to be a stain on the  reputation of britain's biggest police  force  i'm hoping that i will be vindicated  in fact i believe i will be vindicated  the fact that daniel was expressing  repeatedly in the weeks and months and  days before his death concern over  police corruption and then  bang he's dead you know  it it just looks so awful  a private investigator daniel morgan's  job often required him to delve into the  seedier side of london life  [Music]  he'd been here in the golden lion pub in  sydney on the night of march the 10th  1987 for a meeting with his business  partner  it was the last time he was seen alive  we'll probably never know what daniel  morgan discussed inside this pub  shortly before his murder was he as some  have suggested  about to expose local police corruption  whatever the motive even scotland yard  admits the initial investigation into  his death  was hampered by corrupt officers  daniel morgan was attacked as he left to  collect his vehicle from the pub  car park lying in wait his killer  embedded an axe in the back of his head  the 1987 murder investigation was  bungled from the outset daniel morgan's  business partner jonathan reese  and one of the investigating officers  detective sergeant sid fillery  were among six people arrested but later  released without charge  over the years police launched another  five failed investigations  culminating in the dramatic collapse of  a case in 2011  against five men again including  jonathan recent said villarry  to this day they deny any involvement in  daniel morgan's death  and successfully sued the metropolitan  police after the collapse of the trial  the case took another twist when the now  defunct news of the world  placed the lead scotland yard  investigator under surveillance  after he made a fresh appeal to solve  the murder on the bbc's crime watch  program  he and his wife jackie hames a fellow  serving officer at the time  and presenter on crime watch received  anonymous death threats  she still remembers the shock of seeing  people in a van  watching their house it was later  stopped by police  those inside news of the world employees  i can still visualize it to this day the  wind the driver's door window  um came down and i saw something  metal being raised and i just went into  sheer panic i just felt so under threat  and so terrified that i just had to  leave the house  jackie hayes never believed the paper's  assertion that it was investigating  allegations she was having an affair  with chief superintendent david cook the  couple had in fact been  married for years it's her hope and that  of aleister morgan that alleged links  between the tabloid  corrupt police and organized crime will  be fully uncovered  in this long-awaited independent report  but the morgan family have been here  many times before  in their search for the truth over  daniel's murder  mark white sky news
 

